<Base title="About" description="Al Imran's journey from visual communication and advertising to product design, entrepreneurship and research interests.">
<section class="page-hero tone-sage"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><h1>Curious by practice.<br>Intentional by design.</h1><p class="subhead">My career has crossed visual communication, technology and entrepreneurship. I see them as connected ways of understanding people and solving problems.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap two-panel"><div class="long-copy"><p>I studied fine arts with a focus on graphic design at the University of Dhaka. My early professional work in advertising and visual communication sparked an interest in how design shapes perception, trust, and everyday decisions.</p><p>Over time, that interest moved toward user experience, digital products, and designing not just what people see, but what they can understand and do. I later completed postgraduate studies in information technology while continuing to learn through practical work.</p><p>I founded The YOLO Studio to create an environment where strategy, design and technology could meet. Building a company added lessons that classrooms rarely teach: navigating uncertainty, delivering under constraints, and taking responsibility for outcomes.</p><p>Today I am exploring more structured research, particularly in human-computer interaction, digital accessibility, and the adoption of emerging technology in Bangladesh and similar contexts.</p><h2>What I believe</h2><blockquote>Good design should make a difference to the people who use it, not only to the people who present it.</blockquote><p>My work is still evolving. I prefer to show real practice, ongoing questions, and honest limitations rather than exaggerate credentials or outcomes.</p></div><aside class="fact-panel"><p class="tiny-label">AT A GLANCE</p><dl><div class="fact-item"><dt>Primary practice</dt><dd>Design, digital experiences & entrepreneurship</dd></div><div class="fact-item"><dt>Education</dt><dd>Fine Arts (Graphic Design), University of Dhaka; postgraduate information technology studies</dd></div><div class="fact-item"><dt>Professional initiative</dt><dd>Founder, The YOLO Studio</dd></div><div class="fact-item"><dt>Current research direction</dt><dd>Human-computer interaction, accessibility, responsible AI adoption</dd></div><div class="fact-item"><dt>Location</dt><dd>Bangladesh</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div class="sec-label"><span class="sec-number">01 /</span>THE JOURNEY</div><div><h2 class="section-title">Different disciplines. A connected set of questions.</h2><div class="timeline">
<details open><summary><span>01</span><strong>Visual communication & advertising</strong></summary><p>Learning to communicate clearly, shape perception, and create identities that work beyond decoration.</p></details>
<details><summary><span>02</span><strong>Digital product design & user experience</strong></summary><p>Moving from static visuals to interfaces, journeys, interaction decisions, and the needs of actual users.</p></details>
<details><summary><span>03</span><strong>Entrepreneurship & building teams</strong></summary><p>Starting The YOLO Studio and learning what it takes to turn design decisions into real delivery.</p></details>
<details><summary><span>04</span><strong>Technology, accessibility & research</strong></summary><p>Exploring AI-enabled workflows and developing more rigorous ways to investigate accessible, human-centered digital services.</p></details>
</div></div></div></section>
